cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EpiLog in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "EpiLog: A Curated Genomic Safe Harbor Catalog and Post-Edit Silencing Registry"
abstract: >-
  EpiLog is a literature-derived catalog of genomic safe harbor loci and their
  post-editing expression/silencing outcomes, with per-record confidence
  tiers, stability/duration summaries, tissue context, and genome-build
  annotations, spanning human, mouse, dog, pig, goat, cattle, zebrafish, and
  Drosophila melanogaster. It also provides a shared registry for logging new
  gene-editing experiments and tracking silencing status over time.
